--
N5008 [over.match.ctor]/1, [over.match.viable]/2: os() takes no argument, so
for os(&s) only os(buf *) is viable.  The constructors of a class with a
virtual base carry an extra, front-end-internal parameter (a __CPROVER_bool
flag telling whether the virtual base is constructed), and overload
resolution counts it as a real parameter: os() becomes os(bool) and &s
converts to bool, so the call "does not uniquely resolve".  This drops
libc++'s basic_ostringstream constructors (sstream:901, `basic_ostream<
_CharT, _Traits>(&__sb_)'; cpp20_libcxx_header_drops/test_sstream.desc).
Pre-existing (bin53).  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it
fails only its WRONG assertion.
